<title>INDIA: Indian exports rose 8.46 percent in Oct.</title>
<headline>Indian exports rose 8.46 percent in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports increased to $2.68 billion in October, up 8.46 percent from $2.47 billion in the same month in 1995, the government said on Monday.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Oct 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.68	 2.47</p>
<p>    Imports		  3.09	 2.70</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.41	-0.23</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.  </p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports grew 9.91 percent in April-October to $18.91 billion, the statement said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE    Apr-Oct 96	 Apr-Oct 95</p>
<p>    Exports		    18.91		17.20</p>
<p>    Imports		    21.18		19.91</p>
<p>    Trade balance	    -2.28		-2.70</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
</text>
